<title>GERMANY: Rexrodt says certain Germany to meet EMU criteria.</title>
<headline>Rexrodt says certain Germany to meet EMU criteria.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economics Minister Guenter Rexrodt said on Monday he is certain Germany will meet the Maastricht criteria for European monetary union (EMU) on time.</p>
<p>&quot;I am certain we will make it,&quot; he said after a meeting of leaders of his Free Democrats political party, junior partners in Chancellor Helmut Kohl's coalition.</p>
<p>&quot;We need the euro for economic and European policy reasons,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Germany must do all it can to see that the criteria and the time plan are strictly observed, he said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
